# Mary had a baby - traditionele Afro-Amerikaanse spiritual (kerstlied)
# Traditioneel, 19e eeuw; vermoedelijk van de Sea Islands in South Carolina
# (Saint Helena). Volgens de reeks History of Hymns van UMC Discipleship en een
# artikel in The Post and Courier geldt het als traditioneel, zonder bekende maker.
# Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit MARYHADB.ABY (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Tikfouten hersteld: "traine"
# werd "train", "Couns'Ior" werd "Couns'lor". De bron schrijft de middelste
# coupletten af met "enz."; zo overgenomen.
{title: Mary had a baby}
{meta: id mary-had-a-baby}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit MARYHADB.ABY (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via UMC Discipleship (History of Hymns) en The Post and Courier}
{meta: tag geestelijk}
{meta: tag kerst}

{start_of_verse}
Mary had a baby, yes Lord!
Mary had a baby, yes my Lord!
Mary had a baby, yes Lord!
De people keep a com-in' an' train done gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
What did she name him, yes Lord!
What did she name him, yes my Lord!
What did she name him, yes Lord!
De people keep a com-in' an' train done gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
She named him King Jesus
enz.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
She named him Mighty Couns'lor.
enz.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Where was He born
enz.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Mary had a baby, yes Lord!
Mary had a baby, yes my Lord!
Mary had a baby, yes Lord!
Born in a manger
{end_of_verse}
